# Files Docker must NOT send to the build. The build context of every service image is the repo root
# (services/<name>/Dockerfile needs libs/stockline-common too), so without this file "docker build" would upload the
# whole repository first: .git, every target/ folder, node_modules, ... That is slow, and it could put local files
# (.env, IDE settings) into an image layer.
#
# Rule: everything is excluded except libs/ and services/; then build output and IDE files inside them are
# excluded again. A Dockerfile can only COPY what is left.

# 1. Exclude everything (.git, frontend/, docs/, infra/, .history/, .claude/, root files, ...)
*

# 2. Keep the Maven projects
!libs/
!services/

# 3. ...but not their build output, IDE files or secrets
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.idea/
**/*.iml
**/.vscode/
**/.settings/
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.factorypath
**/HELP.md
**/.env
**/.env.*
